                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "42ab0a4c-9009-35dc-9130-3021737bb00d",
                        "entry_id": "3a2734c2-6e7f-3d5a-804f-4d4dc8c40d16",
                        "glosses": [
                            "предаваться пьянству"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "7ae4b641-53a8-4fe1-9e41-1f0f43df645c",
                                "sense_id": "42ab0a4c-9009-35dc-9130-3021737bb00d",
                                "text": "Дворянство пьянствует на белом свете, играет напропалую в карты, дерётся с слугами, развратничает с горничными, ведёт дурно свои дела и ещё хуже семейную жизнь."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "211cbbe8-37fa-444b-b386-77110d277fc5",
                                "sense_id": "42ab0a4c-9009-35dc-9130-3021737bb00d",
                                "text": "Мы не скифы, не люблю, // Други, пьянствовать бесчинно: // Нет, за чашей я пою // Иль беседую невинно."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "23a62b5e-b1a3-4c13-9798-5f6dbacdd827",
                        "source_entry_id": "3a2734c2-6e7f-3d5a-804f-4d4dc8c40d16",
                        "source_sense_id": "42ab0a4c-9009-35dc-9130-3021737bb00d",
                        "target_lang_word": "drink hard",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "a80699d5-a0e4-47df-b64c-1a376bf4c2b2",
                        "source_entry_id": "3a2734c2-6e7f-3d5a-804f-4d4dc8c40d16",
                        "source_sense_id": "42ab0a4c-9009-35dc-9130-3021737bb00d",
                        "target_lang_word": "booze",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "booze",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2affbf47-4c80-34aa-9b7d-cb12cadb85c2",
                                        "entry_id": "41d2c7bd-d93d-36cf-a1d7-aeb5918826d5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any alcoholic beverage (especially beer or hard liquor)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "colloquial",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "65ab14c9-d6c4-4082-adfc-8ebedfe1c825",
                                                "sense_id": "2affbf47-4c80-34aa-9b7d-cb12cadb85c2",
                                                "text": "The glutton castaway, the drunkard in the desert, the lecher in prison, they are the happy ones. To hunger, thirst, lust, every day afresh and every day in vain, after the old prog, the old booze, the old whores, that's the nearest we'll ever get to felicity, the new porch and the very latest garden."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4208346f-3778-401d-8a74-95a254094143",
                                                "sense_id": "2affbf47-4c80-34aa-9b7d-cb12cadb85c2",
                                                "text": "1995, Al Stewart, \"Marion the Chatelaine\" on Between the Wars\nShe got caught between the shadows and the booze\nAnd she surely did know how to have the blues"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a6643b9f-b836-4768-a956-94aeb969b8a2",
                                                "sense_id": "2affbf47-4c80-34aa-9b7d-cb12cadb85c2",
                                                "text": "In some Canadian provinces […] American booze will be pulled off the shelves indefinitely starting on Tuesday."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ae53b702-e39a-36e4-b6fb-88fb5bb743e5",
                                        "entry_id": "41d2c7bd-d93d-36cf-a1d7-aeb5918826d5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A session of drinking alcohol; a drinking party."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "archaic",
                                            "colloquial",
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "booze",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1f448fce-5c7a-3e7c-b34c-4434536f874e",
                                        "entry_id": "34c772a0-1209-3cf4-8b2a-495d6e8879a9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To drink alcohol."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive",
                                            "slang"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3ca37855-a879-41a8-b9c5-70eefbeb7f15",
                                                "sense_id": "1f448fce-5c7a-3e7c-b34c-4434536f874e",
                                                "text": "We were out all night boozing until we dragged ourselves home hung over."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5c903ee4-c534-4db1-b3c2-a9756d78f2f5",
                                                "sense_id": "1f448fce-5c7a-3e7c-b34c-4434536f874e",
                                                "text": "This is better than boozing in public houses."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bc4a4e24-9f1f-3ab6-8265-b4a4d0a92363",
                                        "entry_id": "34c772a0-1209-3cf4-8b2a-495d6e8879a9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To drink (an alcoholic beverage)."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "slang",
                                            "transitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a1f1763b-61c7-43c0-8366-ff3c48bdaff5",
                                                "sense_id": "bc4a4e24-9f1f-3ab6-8265-b4a4d0a92363",
                                                "text": "It's worse than kerosene to boose."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "abd22021-6598-47d3-bc29-6bc48a9c145f",
                        "source_entry_id": "3a2734c2-6e7f-3d5a-804f-4d4dc8c40d16",
                        "source_sense_id": "42ab0a4c-9009-35dc-9130-3021737bb00d",
                        "target_lang_word": "toper",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "toper",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "d24c560e-15e8-386d-8fcd-8125cb8d4f54",
                                        "entry_id": "14049c53-179a-3fba-bb46-1a8d00d83a3d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Someone who drinks alcoholic beverages a lot; a drunkard."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "literary"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "30645eac-bfc0-4050-b085-e9be274af6f7",
                                                "sense_id": "d24c560e-15e8-386d-8fcd-8125cb8d4f54",
                                                "text": "A Toper this! He plied his glass / More strictly than he said the Mass, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a2ef150a-e38f-402e-990a-514baa97c006",
                                                "sense_id": "d24c560e-15e8-386d-8fcd-8125cb8d4f54",
                                                "text": "The liquor soon mounted into their heads, as it generally does even with the arrantest topers newly landed from sea, and they began capering about most obstreperously."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "036452d4-8c78-4f88-af09-2e8a6b4bbcc1",
                                                "sense_id": "d24c560e-15e8-386d-8fcd-8125cb8d4f54",
                                                "text": "[…] Mrs. Irons rebelled in her bed, and refused peremptorily to get up again, to furnish the musical topers with rum and lemons, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fc7b2268-1938-42f2-8f8b-1b8e316aeb7f",
                                                "sense_id": "d24c560e-15e8-386d-8fcd-8125cb8d4f54",
                                                "text": "“Well, if you ask me, Barney is a combination of eight ball, mick, and shonicker,” said McArdle, one of the corner topers."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b547adcb-6f94-422f-8d22-d56abd7645bb",
                                                "sense_id": "d24c560e-15e8-386d-8fcd-8125cb8d4f54",
                                                "text": "George Relph plays the part of the Vicar of the Parish, a railway enthusiast, who becomes amateur engine driver, with Sir Godfrey Tearle (the Bishop) as his fireman, while Stanley Holloway is the genial toper who provides the cash to buy the line."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
